From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sluongng <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jj-lib: Bound line file merging and selected value resolution

Path filtering compares selected values against recursively merged parents.
Calling ordinary file resolution under an async timeout leaves equality,
simplification, diff and materialization work running without a physical bound.

Add separate line-only merge and selected-value APIs that retain stock term
ordering, trivial choices and unresolved values. Charge allocation before
requesting buffers, poll cancellation across comparisons and output copies, and
share one cumulative line budget across calls. Reject word-level merging rather
than falling back to its unbounded implementation. Backend admission remains
caller-owned; read-only queries must supply an ephemeral backend for synthesized
FILE writes. Existing ordinary APIs are unchanged.
---
